{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3em74uq2Mtd5GVrBeg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I split the system prompt into two cached blocks in `bot.py`, so a `save_fact` rewrite only changes the second block. The static block may still be too small for the cache to use, though.\n\n`build_system` used to send one block with one `cache_control` marker. Any new fact changed that block, so the whole prefix missed. That matches the usage log: after each `save_fact`, `cache_read` is 0 and `cache_creation` is about 1000 again.\n\nIt now sends two blocks, each with its own marker:\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, which is identical for every user and day.\n2. The athlete context: date, profile, zones, goal, facts and language.\n\nI checked offline that appending a fact leaves block 1 unchanged and only changes block 2. I did not call the API, so the effect on real `cache_read` and `cache_creation` numbers is untested.\n\nMy estimate for the static part (instructions plus the core tools) is about 730 tokens. Sonnet 4.5 needs at least 1024 tokens before a breakpoint, so the first marker may be ignored. If so, a memory write would still re-create the whole prompt. To check, send a message after a `save_fact` and look at `logs/usage.jsonl`. `cache_read` should be about 730 or more and `cache_creation` only the tail, about 300. If `cache_read` is 0, the options are to add real coaching content to the static block or to change model. I didn't pad it with invented rules.\n\nFrom your colleague's note I used the two-marker split, kept the static block free of dates and counters, left the tools array alone, and checked `usage`. I skipped top-N fact selection, since the bot already loads all facts, and the tool filtering, which already exists. I also didn't carry over its token counts, which don't match this prompt.\n\n`ANSWER.md` records this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,